   752	   smooth numbers in the |Δ| lift classes of a reduced residue to moduli ℓ²nq. Here n is B-smooth,
   753	   q ≤ 2S², the moduli are ≍ N^{s+3/(4k)}L^{O(1)}, and the values are ≍ N^{s+h+d/(4k)}.
   754	2. **LV6** (bookkeeping of a known method at new heights; not expected to need a new idea, but not
   755	   written).
   756	
   757	Within this project's proved results, nothing else is missing. FM, the binary rational correlation,
   758	the kernel transfer, the split counting (Theorem S′), the complete-target-list reduction (Theorem K)
   759	and fruitfulness (DD) are proved here or in hypD/lemmaM.
   760	
   761	Caveats:
   762	- these are internal, unrefereed results;
   763	- the HECM running-time theorem (Theorem A only; A′ avoids it);
   764	- the Lemma 5.1 irreducibility transfer, checked at the level of statements.
   765	
   766	**Has anyone beaten c = 1 rigorously (1992–2026)?** To our knowledge, no. Codex pcest_1 and pcest_2 and
   767	the Opus literature critic (§7) all searched. Neither found a rigorous algorithm factoring every N in L[1/2, c] with c < 1. The
   768	rigorous record remains Lenstra–Pomerance 1992 (JAMS 5, 483–516).
   769	- Related results are either heuristic (NFS; Stange 2022) or concern other problems:
   770	  - Kleinjung–Wesolowski: discrete logarithms in finite fields of fixed characteristic (JAMS 35, 2022).
   771	  - de Boer–Pellet-Mary–Wesolowski (arXiv 2512.01588): ERH, class and unit groups.
   772	- Under GRH the best rigorous constant is also c = 1: Seysen and A. K. Lenstra's class-group method,
   773	  whose GRH dependence Lenstra–Pomerance removed. We know of no c < 1 under a standard hypothesis.
   774	- Lee–Venkatesan (J. Number Theory 187 (2018) 92–159) produce congruences in L[1/3], but their
   775	  factoring conclusion is
   776	  conditional on their Conjecture 7.1.
   777	- This is a search result, not a certification.
