   517	## 4. PC_alg: the kernel transfer, the remaining hypothesis, and why known tools fall short
   518	
   519	### 4.1 Lemma Kern (the 2D kernel lemma) [proved; tested]
   520	
   521	**Setup.** Let d ≥ 3, and let P ≠ P′ be primitive with |P|, |P′| ∈ [V/2, √2V] and Δ = det(P, P′) ≠ 0.
   522	Put v = v(P), v′ = v(P′), and Φ: Z^d → Z², c ↦ (⟨c, v⟩, ⟨c, v′⟩). Write P′ ≡ κP (mod Δ); κ exists
   523	because P is primitive.
   524	
   525	**Statement.**
   526	- (i) Γ := Φ(Z^d) has index |Δ| and equals {(X, X′) : X′ ≡ κ^{d−1}X (mod Δ)}.
   527	- (ii) ker Φ = Q_{PP′}·Z[x, y]_{d−3}, where Q_{PP′} = (bx − ay)(b′x − a′y). This kernel is saturated, and
   528	  its monomial basis has ‖·‖_∞ ≤ 2V².
   529	- (iii) If H ≥ V², then for every z ∈ Z²,
   530	    Pr_{c∈C_H}[Φ(c) = z] ≤ C_d·|Δ|/(H²‖v ∧ v′‖) ≤ C′_d/(H²V^{2d−4}).
   531	
   532	*Proof.*
   533	- **(ii).** ⟨c, v(P)⟩ = C(P) for the form C = Σ c_i x^{d−1−i}y^i. C(P) = 0 with P primitive gives
   534	  (bx − ay) | C over Z, by Gauss's lemma. Then C(P′) = 0 and det(P, P′) ≠ 0 give (b′x − a′y) | C/(bx − ay).
   535	  So ker Φ = Q·Z[x, y]_{d−3}. A multiple of Q that is integral is an integral multiple, again by Gauss's
   536	  lemma, so the kernel is saturated.
   537	- **(i).** The index of Φ(Z^d) is the gcd of the 2×2 minors of [v; v′], which is |Δ| (hypD Prop G(i),
   538	  (I6); also codex pcest_1, via a unimodular change sending P to (1, 0)). Since P′ ≡ κP (mod Δ),
   539	  v′ ≡ κ^{d−1}v (mod Δ), so Γ lies in the displayed lattice, which also has index |Δ|. Hence they are
   540	  equal.
   541	- **(iii).**
   542	  - A fibre is (c₀ + K) ∩ C_H, with K = ker Φ of rank d − 2 and det K = ‖v ∧ v′‖/|Δ|. Here we use that
   543	    a saturated lattice and its orthogonal complement in Z^d have the same determinant, and that the row
   544	    lattice of [v; v′] has index |Δ| in its saturation.
   545	  - The translates c + F, where F is the fundamental cell of the basis in (ii), are disjoint. They lie
   546	    in the section of the cube [−(2d−3)H, (2d−3)H]^d by a (d−2)-flat, whose volume is ≤ C_dH^{d−2}.
   547	  - So the fibre has ≤ C_dH^{d−2}|Δ|/‖v ∧ v′‖ points. Divide by (2H + 1)^d.
   548	  - For the second inequality: every 2×2 minor of [v; v′] equals Δ·W_{ij}(P, P′), with W bihomogeneous
   549	    of bidegree (d−2, d−2). For example W_{01} = (aa′)^{d−2}.
   550	  - The vector W(P, P′) of all divided minors never vanishes on (S¹)² (repaired after codex pcest_2).
   551	    - Off the diagonal and antidiagonal, this is injectivity of the projective Veronese map: v(P) ∦ v(P′)
   552	      when P ∦ P′, and Δ ≠ 0.
   553	    - On the diagonal, W(P, P) is the wedge of v(P) with its tangent ∂_u v(P) divided by det(P, u). It
   554	      is nonzero because the rational normal curve is nondegenerate. For example, at P = (1, 0) the
   555	      adjacent divided minor W_{01} equals 1. The antidiagonal is the same up to sign.
   556	    - W is continuous, so by compactness ‖v ∧ v′‖ ≥ c_d|Δ|(|P||P′|)^{d−2}. ∎
   557	    - The exact identity det K·|Δ| = ‖v ∧ v′‖ and the bound with c_d > 0.05 (d ≤ 7) are checked exactly
   558	      in `tests/test_pcest.py`.
   559	
   560	*Cost [proved arithmetic].*
   561	- H ≥ V² = ℓS² means h > 1/(2k), which raises the h-floor from LV's 1/(4k) (FM) to 1/(2k).
   562	- Then θ = 2s + (d−1)/(4k) + max(1/(2k), s − (d−2)/(4k)). The floor binds only for k < d(d+1)/4,
   563	  against (d² − 1)/4 before.
   564	- **The infimum over k is unchanged.**
   565	- Finite-k examples: d = 9, k = 20 gives θ = 0.325 instead of 0.3125, so c = 0.937 instead of 0.928. At
   566	  d = 9 the minimal k with c < 1 moves from 11 to 12 (`src/pcest/params.py`). Codex's (5) agrees.
   567	- If one also wanted the moduli G|Δ to stay below |F|^{1/2} (not needed below), the condition would
   568	  become h > s + (6 − d)/(4k) (codex).
   569	
   570	### 4.2 Reduction of PC to one arithmetic hypothesis
   571	
   572	**Notation.** For a pair (P, P′) ∈ 𝒫_ℓ² with ℓ | Δ, and g ∈ 𝒢 ∩ L_ℓ(P):
   573	- G = G_g(P), G′ = G_g(P′), and T := dHV^{d−1};
   574	- the full windows I := F̂_g(P) + G·[−T, T] and I′ likewise;
   575	- the lift classes r_j := F̂_g(P) + Gj (mod G|Δ|) and r′_j := F̂_g(P′) + G′κ^{d−1}j (mod G′|Δ|), for
   576	  j mod |Δ|.
   577	
   578	**The normalized lift correlation.**
   579	  κ_alg(ℓ, P, P′, g) := |Δ|·Σ_{j mod |Δ|} Ψ_I(G|Δ|, r_j)·Ψ_{I′}(G′|Δ|, r′_j) / (4T²·ϱ(T|G|, B)·ϱ(T|G′|, B)),
   580	where Ψ_I(m, r) := #{F ∈ I ∩ 𝒮_B : F ≡ r (mod m)}. If the smooth numbers of each window were spread
   581	evenly over the |Δ| lift classes, κ_alg would be ≍ 1.
   582	
   583	**Prop 4.2 [proved].** Assume h ≥ 1/(2k) + η₀. For each such (ℓ, P, P′, g),
   584	  Pr_c[F_A(P), F_A(P′) ∈ 𝒮_B] ≤ C_d·(V²/|Δ|)·ϱ(T|G|)ϱ(T|G′|)·κ_alg.
   585	*Proof.*
   586	- By Lemma Kern(iii), Pr_c ≤ C′_d(H²V^{2d−4})^{−1}·#{z ∈ Γ ∩ [−T, T]² : F̂ + Gz₁ and F̂′ + G′z₂ smooth}.
   587	- By Lemma Kern(i), that count is Σ_j Ψ_I(G|Δ|, r_j)Ψ_{I′}(G′|Δ|, r′_j).
   588	- Insert the definition of κ_alg and T² = d²H²V^{2d−2}. ∎
   589	
   590	Here V²/|Δ| = S²/q is comparable to (not equal to) the bounding-box factor 1/sin∠(P, P′).
   591	- If κ_alg were ≤ L^{o(1)}, the factor would cost only O(log S) on average. For fixed P and q, the
   592	  equation det(P, P′) = ±ℓq has O(1) solutions P′ in the box (they lie on two lines parallel to P,
   593	  spaced by |P| ≥ V/2).
   594	- So Σ over pairs of (S²/q)·(Theorem R's uniform per-pair bound) loses only a harmonic sum
   595	  Σ_{q≤2S²} 1/q.
   596	- LD keeps the product (S²/q)·κ_alg; the two factors are not separated.
   597	
   598	**Hypothesis LD (lift dispersion under rational-smoothness weights) [open].** Uniformly in N:
   599	  E_ℓ Σ_{P≠P′, ℓ|Δ} |𝒢|^{−1} Σ_{g∈𝒢∩L_ℓ(P)} Y_PY_{P′}·(S²/q)·κ_alg ≤ L^{o(1)}·E_ℓ Σ_{P≠P′, ℓ|Δ} |𝒢|^{−1} Σ_g Y_PY_{P′}.
   600	- It is an upper bound, at precision L^{o(1)}, for a restricted second moment of smooth numbers in the
   601	  lift classes of moving residues to moduli G|Δ| = ℓ²nq.
   602	- The weights are the actual rational-smooth multiplicities. Theorem R shows that the right side is
   603	  ≤ (log N)^{O(1)}S⁴ρ_r².
   604	- LD is implied by a suitably weighted form of hypD's RBDH′ (an o(1) relative variance), but it is
   605	  *weaker*: it is an upper bound within L^{o(1)}. It is codex pcest_1's (6) with the kernel transfer
   606	  carried out. We do not claim an equivalence.
   607	
   608	**Theorem 4.3 [proved implication; repaired after codex pcest_2].**
   609	- **Hypotheses.** Those of Theorem FM, with h ≥ 1/(2k) + η₀ and S² := (log N)^{C₃}/(ρ_rρ_F), where C₃ is
   610	  larger than the polylog exponent lost in Theorem FM. Let N_ℓ(A) be the **filtered** count of §1
   611	  (|G(P)| ≥ MV/32).
   612	- **Conclusions.**
   613	  - (i) FM + Theorem R + Prop 4.2 + LD ⟹ PC := E[N(N−1)]/(E N)² ≤ L^{o(1)}.
   614	  - (ii) Hence, by Prop PZ (E N ≥ 1), D_k(γ) holds with γ ≥ L^{−o(1)}.
