   181	**Counted candidates and the capped search.**
   182	- Put 𝒫_ℓ := {(a, b) : b prime, V/2 < b ≤ V, |a| ≤ V, gcd(a, b) = 1}, and
   183	  Λ_ℓ(g) := {P : ℓ | G(P)}, which has index ℓ when ℓ ∤ g₁.
   184	- The search enumerates Λ_ℓ(g) ∩ [−V, V]² from a Gauss-reduced basis, tests membership in 𝒫_ℓ, and
   185	  tests G(P)/ℓ and F_A(P) for B-smoothness.
   186	  - Primality of b uses a deterministic polynomial-time test (AKS).
   187	  - Smoothness is tested by HECM, as in LV Cor. 3.19.
   188	- N_ℓ(A) := #{P ∈ 𝒫_ℓ ∩ Λ_ℓ(g) : |G(P)| ≥ MV/32, G(P)/ℓ ∈ 𝒮_B, F_A(P) ∈ 𝒮_B}. Each such P is a
   189	  certified descent relation. ℓ² ∤ G(P) holds automatically, because ℓ > B.
   190	  - The **filter |G(P)| ≥ MV/32** was added after codex pcest_2 (§7.2). Without it, candidates with
   191	    |G| as small as ℓ have algebraic values smaller by a polynomial factor. Their smoothness density
   192	    can then exceed ρ_F by L^{Θ(1)}, which breaks Theorem 4.3's comparison. FM only ever uses
   193	    |G| ∈ [MV/32, 2MV], so the filter costs nothing there.
   194	  - A capped randomized smoothness test is repeated O(log N) times, so that a smooth value is
   195	    recognized with probability ≥ 1 − N^{−2}. This costs a polylogarithmic factor.
   196	- **Lemma 1.3 (regularity) [proved].** Suppose λ₁(Λ_ℓ(g)) < √ℓ/(2S), attained at w. Then
   197	  Λ_ℓ(g) ∩ 𝒫_ℓ = ∅. Otherwise #(Λ_ℓ(g) ∩ [−V, V]²) ≤ C_abs·S² for an absolute constant C_abs (e.g. 100).
   198	  *Proof.*
   199	  - w is primitive in Z²: its content e satisfies e ≤ |w| < ℓ, so gcd(e, ℓ) = 1 and w/e ∈ Λ_ℓ(g); by
   200	    minimality e = 1.
   201	  - So w is primitive in Λ_ℓ(g) (index ℓ), and the lattice is the union of the lines jw′ + Zw, j ∈ Z,
   202	    which are parallel to w at mutual distance ℓ/|w| > 2V.
   203	  - Every point of [−V, V]² has norm ≤ √2V < 2V, so it lies on the central line Zw. The only primitive
   204	    points there are ±w, and |w| < V/2 < b for every point of 𝒫_ℓ.
   205	  - In the regular case take a reduced basis (λ₁ ≤ λ₂, λ₁λ₂ ≤ (2/√3)ℓ). The translates of the
   206	    fundamental cell F at the lattice points of K = [−V, V]² are disjoint and lie in K + F. So the count
   207	    is ≤ (area(K) + perimeter(K)·diam F + π diam(F)²)/ℓ ≤ 4S² + O(V/λ₁) + O(λ₂/λ₁) ≤ C_abs S², using
   208	    λ₁ ≥ √ℓ/(2S), V/λ₁ ≤ 2S² and λ₂/λ₁ ≤ (2/√3)ℓ/λ₁² ≤ 8S²/√3. ∎
   209	- So the cap T_SQ := C_abs S²·(log N)^{O(1)} is never binding on a lattice that contains a candidate.
   210	  Irregular lattices need no separate exclusion: they contribute nothing.
   211	
   212	**Sizes [proved arithmetic].** For P ∈ 𝒫_ℓ and g ∈ 𝒢:
   213	- |G(P)| ≤ 2MV, so |G/ℓ| ≤ X_r := 2MV/ℓ = N^{s−1/(4k)}L^{O(1)};
   214	- |F̂_g(P)| = O_d(MV^d);
   215	- |G(P)⟨c, v(P)⟩| ≤ 2dMHV^d, so |F_A(P)| ≤ X_F := C_d MHV^d = N^{s+h+d/(4k)}L^{O(1)}.
   216	
   217	With ρ_r := ϱ(X_r, B) and ρ_F := ϱ(X_F, B), these are exactly hypD's exponents, so
   218	θ = 2s + h + (d−1)/(4k) as in `src/pcest/params.py`.
