   819	
   820	Command (as registered):
   821	`.venv/bin/python -m src.pcest.e1 experiments/configs/pcest_e1.json experiments/raw/pcest_e1.jsonl 8`,
   822	then `--analyze` (summary in `experiments/raw/pcest_e1_summary.json`).
   823	- Setup: 8 instances (semi/tri × 56/64 bits × seeds 0, 1), 40 fields × 30 primes ℓ ∈ (2¹¹, 2¹²] per
   824	  design, d = 3, S = 16, B_rat = 256, B_alg = 16384, H = 1024.
   825	
   826	| prediction | registered | result |
   827	|---|---|---|
   828	| P1 PC_rat(2D) | [0.8, 1.5] in ≥ 7/8 | 1.007–1.013 in 8/8 — holds |
   829	| P2 PC(2D) | [0.8, 2.0] in ≥ 7/8 | 1.059–1.282 in 8/8 — holds |
   830	| P3 \|PC_rat(2D) − PC_rat(1D)\| | ≤ 0.25 in ≥ 7/8 | ≤ 0.003 in 8/8 — holds |
   831	| P4 E N(2D)/E N(1D) | [0.7, 1.4] in ≥ 7/8 | 0.766–0.938 in 8/8 — holds |
   832	| P5 exact identities | 0 violations | 0 identity violations; 160/160 Lemma Q checks pass (see disclosure) |
   833	| P6 (reported) | — | γ(2D) 0.68–0.89 vs γ(1D) 0.75–0.92; PC_alg(2D) 1.05–1.27 vs PC_alg(1D) 1.06–1.14 |
   834	
   835	**Disclosure (P5).** The harness counts "G = 0 or ℓ ∤ G" as a violation, and flagged 1 event in each of
   836	3 one-dimensional records.
   837	- In each case m ≡ 0 (mod ℓ). Then the lattice {a ≡ 0 (mod ℓ)} is irregular (λ₁ = 1), and its box
   838	  contains the root point (m, 1), where G = a − m b = 0.
   839	- These are degenerate points of irregular lattices, which the theory excludes (Lemma 1.3), and the
   840	  code skips them. They are not failures of ℓ | G or of Lemma 1.2.
   841	- Factor discoveries: none were possible, by construction. Every prime factor of the instances
   842	  (≥ 2¹⁸) exceeds ℓ and both smoothness bounds, so gcd(G, N) = gcd(F, N) = 1 for every tested smooth
   843	  value. STRUCTURAL and ACCIDENTAL rates are both 0, with null expectation 0.
   844	
   845	**Reading.**
   846	- The 2D design yields about 14% fewer pairs. Its rational values g₁a − g₀b are larger by a constant
   847	  factor than a − bm.
   848	- Its correlations are indistinguishable from the 1D design's at toy size.
   849	- PC_rat ≈ 1.01 reflects large E N_rat (130–190) at these bounds. The toy is not informative about the
   850	  asymptotic difficulty of PC_rat in 1D, which is a question of provability, not of size.
   851	- PC_alg ≈ 1.1–1.3 is consistent with hypD E2 (1.08–1.21). This is weak support that LD is true; it is
   852	  not evidence for any asymptotic statement.
